From e1dfd314874109b9cb2622d512375596ea0c846f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:13:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 167/182] hydra: Cycles AOVs LOP, Blender's View Layer passes
 as render vars

A digital asset laid out like Blender's View Layer page (Data, Light,
Cryptomatte, Shader AOVs, Light Groups). Each checked pass becomes a
UsdRenderVar named and written as Blender names it (DiffDir, IndexOB,
CryptoObject00, Combined_<group>...), sourcing the Cycles pass the
delegate resolves, and is appended to the render products: the ones
named on the node, or those of the stage's render settings. The vars go
next to the first product, since Karma's /Render may be deactivated.
